As a Weekend Assembly Operator, you will work independently in a structured, high-tech cleanroom environment where precision and attention to detail are essential. Your technical experience and ability to learn quickly will help you to assemble delicate, high-tech products and perform cleaning and other assembly-related tasks while following strict cleanroom procedures and quality standards. You will play an important role in keeping production areas clean, safe, and contamination-free.

Your responsibilities include:

- Working accurately and with attention to detail;
- Being able to read and understand technical drawings;
- Being able to work effectively in a structured environment;
- Being available to work every weekend, at least until January 2027:
- Having technical experience in assembly;
- Being a fast learner and able to quickly pick up new tasks and procedures.

Working hours:

- Every Saturday and Sunday: approximately 06:00–18:00 (11-hour shifts).

- English level B1–B2;
- Be available to work every Saturday and Sunday from 06:00 to 18:00;
- Feel comfortable working in a cleanroom environment;
- Be flexible, reliable, and able to work independently;
- Be able to follow strict cleanroom rules, procedures, and technical instructions;
- Have experience with assembly or technical assembly work;
- Be able to understand and follow technical instructions accurately.
